{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Reuben, you are my firstborn.</b> The metrical structure of this verse is: \"Reuben, you are my firstborn, and my strength, and the first of my might; the excellency of my exaltation, and the excellency of my strength.\" Its meaning is: You are the firstborn of my strength and the first of my might, in that I was in the preeminence of exaltation and dignity, as in the language of \"Will not His exaltation make you afraid?\" (Job 13:11), \"At His exaltation the mighty ones are afraid\" (ibid. 41:17) — meaning loftiness and greatness — and in that He gives preeminence of strength for war, as in \"and He will give strength to His king\" (I Samuel 2:10), and \"strong in war\" (Isaiah 42:25)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:46:40.484870905Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}